\
<rgb=#FF0000>You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests.</rgb>"},
[6462]={"Lleva el bloque de hielo al puesto de crema dulce helada","¡Una anciana bloquea tu camino! Debes esperar a que pase...","El bloque de hielo que hay que entregar en Delagua se encuentra en el Árbol de la Fiesta.\
\
Lleva el hielo al puesto de crema dulce helada en Delagua.","¡Un niño bloquea tu camino! Debes esperar a que pase...","Tansy Campotieso te ha pedido que entregues un bloque de hielo a la vendedora de crema dulce helada en Delagua. ¡Asegúrate de esquivar los obstáculos!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada.</rgb>","'¡Gracias! Hace ya un rato que se me acabó el hielo, y toda esta gente está esperando su crema dulce helada. Ahora puedo volver a trabajar.'","¡Un anciano bloquea tu camino! Debes esperar a que pase...","Entrega de hielo","Le has entregado el hielo a la vendedora de postres","¡Un gato bloquea tu camino! Debes esperar a que pase...","Bluet Valeoro está en su puesto de venta en Delagua.\
\
Habla con Bluet Valeoro.","Habla con Bluet Valeoro","'¿Has visitado el puesto en Delagua que vende crema dulce helada? Es una delicia, pero la vendedora continuamente necesita hielo de nuestro almacén cubierto aquí en Hobbiton, ya que se derretiría si lo lleváramos todo a Delagua de una vez.\
\
'Lo único que se puede hacer es llevar un bloque cada día. A mí me resulta demasiado pesado, pero tú pareces fuerte. ¿Te importaría llevarlo?\
\
'Solo ten cuidado con los obstáculos. La gente se mueve despacio y se interpone en el camino, y el hielo te dificultará la visión...'"},
[6463]={"'Gracias a ti, los Vesi-henki han sido honrados como es debido. Te estoy agradecido.'","Regresa con Kimmo a Pynti-peldot","'Excelente trabajo. Sé que no ha sido un viaje fácil, pero has prestado un gran servicio a Pynti-peldot.'","Hielo al borde del agua","El santuario lossoth se encuentra a lo largo de la orilla de la Bahía Helada, al oeste y al norte de Pynti-peldot, más allá y cuesta abajo de las ruinas enanas conocidas como las Piedras Solitarias.\
\
Kimmo te ha pedido que encuentres el santuario lossoth dedicado al espíritu del agua y coloques la estatuilla sobre su pedestal antes de que se derrita.","Kimmo el artista desea hacer una ofrenda a los espíritus del agua en nombre de la gente de Pynti-peldot.","Coloca la estatuilla de hielo en el santuario del espíritu del agua","La estatuilla se ha derretido en tu mochila","Informa a Kimmo en Pynti-peldot de que has colocado correctamente la estatuilla.","'Hay un lugar en el borde de la Bahía Helada que es sagrado para los Vesi-henki. Es tradición dejar allí una estatuilla de hielo tallada como súplica para que los espíritus concedan su bendición sobre el clima y la caza.\
\
'He tallado la estatuilla y la he conservado en el frío para que no se derrita, pero ya no soy tan joven como antes. ¿Podrías llevarla hasta el lugar que le corresponde? Tendrás que darte prisa, pues el calor de tu cuerpo hará que se derrita en tu mochila si tardas demasiado.\
\
'Sigue la orilla del agua hacia el oeste y el norte, atravesando las antiguas ruinas conocidas como las Piedras Solitarias, y encontrarás un sendero que desciende desde ellas hasta el mismísimo borde del agua. ¡Ten cuidado con las bestias del camino y con la mordedura mortal de la Bahía!'","'Sigue el borde del agua junto al acantilado hacia el oeste y el norte, atravesando las antiguas ruinas enanas conocidas como las Piedras Solitarias, y encontrarás un sendero que desciende desde ellas hasta el mismo borde del agua. Allí hallarás el santuario de los Vesi-henki. ¡Date prisa! La estatuilla se derretirá y será una pobre ofrenda si tardas demasiado.'"},
[6464]={"Forja un Ícono de los Héroes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega un Ícono de los Héroes a Hróar en Gath Forthnír","El Concilio del Norte necesita una medalla para entregar a los héroes que han caído al servicio de los Pueblos Libres.","Ícono de los Héroes — Introducción","'Una vez más, has prestado un servicio valioso. Estoy a tu servicio... y al de tu familia.'","Hróar está en Gath Forthnír, en Angmar.\
\
Hróar te ha pedido que forjes un Ícono de los Héroes y se lo lleves.","'Nuestra distinción más alta para quienes han caído en actos de valentía ignorada al servicio de los Pueblos Libres es el Ícono de los Héroes. Por desgracia, el artesano talentoso que lo creó incluyó materiales raros y difíciles de obtener, y aquí tenemos muy poco para trabajar. Si pudieras encontrar los materiales necesarios y forjar un Ícono de los Héroes, te estaríamos profundamente agradecidos.\
\
'¿Quién sabe? Si sigues demostrando tu valía, quizá algún día un Ícono así repose sobre tu pecho cuando te bajemos a tu tumba... una idea de lo más reconfortante, ¿no crees?'"},
[6465]={"Idle Longbeard explorers can be found along the western shore of Durthuzâram near Lugun-nâla and at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
Believing it disrespectful, Spall has asked you to tell the dwarves to stop casting stones into Durthuzâram.","Tell idle Longbeard explorers to stop casting stones into Durthuzâram (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Ah, but before you go, have you seen those dwarves casting stones into the Gloomingtarn? And Longbeards, no less. To desecrate the caverns where Durin the Deathless first awoke and in such a manner—it is unthinkable!\
\
'I would be of a mind to reprimand them myself, but it seems I've already made something of a reputation for myself among the dwarves of Lord Stormhammer's expedition. Why, I've even overheard them call me names! Spall the Stuffy, they call me. Better stuffy than disrespectful, I say!\
\
'Even so, something must be done. Would you tell those dwarves to stop casting stones into Durthuzâram? There will be time enough for idle amusement when the Mountain-home is reclaimed!'","Told idle Longbeard explorers to stop casting stones into Durthuzâram (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Spall can be found at Lugun-nâla in Gloomingtarn.\
\
You have told several idle Longbeard explorers to stop casting stones into Durthuzâram. You should return to Spall.","Idle Discourtesies","'They've stopped? Very good! You are held in high regard by Prince Durin, and I knew they would listen to you... even if they disagreed with my reasoning.\
\
'I appreciate you doing that on my behalf, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Spall at Lugun-nâla","Believing it to be disrespectful to the site where Durin the Deathless first awoke, Spall has resolved to stop idle Longbeards from casting stones into the Gloomingtarn."},
[6466]={"Talk to Ioreth in the High Hall","'Have you a moment, ${PLAYER}? \
\
'With such a journey ahead, I count myself and this host fortunate to have you here at my side. Yet my thoughts stray back to Minas Tirith... and to those we left behind. Many dear friends and strangers alike now fight their own battles against illness and injury.\
\
'It was with great sadness that I could not tend to them all, but the greater matters of the Dark Lord and the Ring-bearer's hidden quest have called me away. I know not if I shall ever return to Minas Tirith, and I worry for the fates of those we left behind if I fall in our final gambit.\
\
'Do you remember the Master Herbalist we encountered during my brief time in the City? The one called Galathir? He was unfit for his post and could have caused great harm to those in his care, but I had not the means to send him from the Houses of Healing... not without declaring myself.\
\
'I ask that you return to the Houses of Healing in Minas Tirith and speak with the healer Ioreth. Ensure that she keeps Galathir's ruinous tinctures from the wounded, and have her be my eyes in the High Hall. \
\
'She will heed my words, even if they are delivered in my stead. You are one of the swiftest riders among my ranks, and I entrust this task to you alone.\
\
'Go with haste, my friend. Once you have returned, we can continue planning our course into the Wastes.'","Idle Hands","On the eve of his final assault against the Dark Lord, Aragorn's thoughts turn to Minas Tirith and the wounded.","Ioreth can be found in the High Hall within the Masters' Tier of Minas Tirith (After-battle).\
\
Aragorn has asked you to return to Minas Tirith and learn of the fates of the wounded as well as what further havoc may have been wrought by Galathir's overeager hands.","'You have come at the request of the king?'\
\
You inform Ioreth that Aragorn has not yet claimed that title, and then tell her of his concerns about Galathir's healing practices.\
\
'Whether he claims the title or not, I know him for what he is. He has the hands of a healer, and none but a king could work kingsfoil into such a potent medicine - and I would know! Still, it troubles me that he has grown concerned about Galathir's methods. Not precisely because I disagree, mind you, but because I did not think it would be so plainly noticed!\
\
'I cannot send Galathir away, but I can help prevent him from treating any more of the wounded with Everworth. It is the least I can do for my king!\
\
'However, there remains one other matter of concern regarding Galathir... and his new apprentice.'"},
[6467]={"'Stop! No one is allowed through here.\
\
'You want to be allowed entrance here? I do not care if the Elders themselves... \
\
'They did? \
\
'Nevertheless, you need to prove yourself to me. I am the Keeper of the Cave. Before you enter, you must clear the land of the foul monsters. Return when you are done, and you may safely pass.'","'Well done. You have completed the Task of the Keeper. You may pass.'","Defeat dun-crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Win at the entrance to the Pristine Glade","River-turtles and dun-crows roam the lands outside the cave to the Pristine Glade.\
\
Win has asked you to defeat foul monsters outside the cave entrance to the Pristine Glade to earn his trust. The only monsters, however, are river-turtles and dun-crows.","Win is at the entrance to the Pristine Glade.\
\
You should return to Win at the cave entrance and tell him the deed is done.","Defeated river-turtles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","If It is not Too Much Trouble","Defeat river-turtles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Defeat the turtles and crebain, and I may permit you entrance to the Glade.'","Defeated dun-crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Protectors of the Pristine Glade need your help defending the Glade from invaders."},
[6470]={"Report to Captain Róglarg","Ignoble Duties","After disguising yourself as the Silent One, you have come to realize that the duties of the Orcs of Cirith Ungol now fall to you.","Captain Róglarg can be found in the courtyard of Cirith Ungol. Práguk, Krúrglok, Lúksu, Danghát, and Shíkurz can be found throughout Cirith Ungol.\
\
Captain Róglarg has asked you to take over the duties of the Orcs that were slain in Dath Nethryn. You should speak to other Orcs in Cirith Ungol and learn what needs to be done.","Performed the Silent One's duties in Cirith Ungol (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'All of them? Really now?'\
\
You nod.\
\
'I'm impressed, Silent One. Turning a new leaf, are you? Well, keep it turned.\
\
'The Top Ones want this place to look like it did before Lugbúrz caved in on itself. Between Cirith Ungol and Durthang, we've got to find a way to keep those tarks out of Mordor!\
\
'Ah, but it's not just the tarks, is it?'","'Ah, but now that you're back, I've got some work for you!\
\
'We lost a couple more Orcs this morning in the swamp, so more work's got to fall onto less backs. And I think it ought to be yours, Silent One!\
\
'Some have even been complaining that those Orcs shirked their duties by dying. Isn't that a shame? Well, it's all got to get done. The High Up sent a nosy Man to watch our backs, and I won't be made to look a fool like Shagrat!\
\
'See what Práguk, Krúrglok, Lúksu, Danghát, and Shíkurz want, but don't go far. I have plenty of work for you, too!\
\
'Now, unless I tell you otherwise, there's no need to report back to me or any of that lot. Believe me, I'll know if you didn't follow my orders, Silent One....\
\
'Hah! Good to be back, eh?'","Perform the Silent One's duties in Cirith Ungol (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Captain Róglarg can be found in the courtyard of Cirith Ungol.\
\
You have finished every task laid before you as the Silent One, and should now report back to Captain Róglarg."},
